{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785306157248,"sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_0vcmZuy42sYMkBFZgTbSlKF6","state":{"status":"error","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\n - [ ] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\n - [ ] Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\n - [ ] Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short?\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n-[None yet]\n+- [x] What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them? (iteration 1)\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n-[None yet]\n+- Contract-driven inventory bounded the JSON universe before counting files. (iteration 1)\n+- Direct root-gate and freshness-gate execution established current fleet state. (iteration 1)\n+- Consumer and generator tracing separated root identity from advisor projections. (iteration 1)\n@@\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n-[None yet]\n+- Broad filename discovery mixed unrelated spec-folder continuity JSON with skill-root identity JSON. (iteration 1)\n@@\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n-[None yet]\n+- Treat spec-folder `generate-description.js` and `backfill-graph-metadata.js` as skill-root producers; they own a separate schema. (iteration 1)\n+- Treat `ci-leaf-manifest-freshness.cjs` as complete fleet-adoption coverage; it discovers committed outputs rather than all `SKILL.md` roots. (iteration 1)\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Dimension 1, inventory and current state: enumerate every in-scope JSON type, classify authored versus generated, measure presence per H or S root, and map current generation and validation coverage.\n+Dimension 2, optimization: identify redundant or unused fields, duplicate representations, drift-prone data, consolidation candidates, and fields with no verified consumer across root metadata, advisor projections, and compiled routes.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n@@\n   \"openQuestions\": [\n-    \"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\",\n     \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n@@\n-  \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n-  \"keyFindings\": [],\n-  \"ruledOutDirections\": [],\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n+    {\n+      \"question\": \"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\",\n+      \"iteration\": 1,\n+      \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-001.md\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"keyFindings\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f1\",\"summary\":\"Eight governed root JSON filenames split across H and S with class-specific authored/generated status.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f2\",\"summary\":\"The current fleet has seven H and four S roots; all 11 pass root-contract and generated-freshness gates.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f3\",\"summary\":\"graph-metadata.json is authored identity with a separately generated advisor-maintained derived block.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f4\",\"summary\":\"Scaffolds emit authored declarations while the root gate owns derivable manifest and S-alias generation.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f5\",\"summary\":\"The root gate has complete adoption discovery while the older freshness scanner sees committed manifests only.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f6\",\"summary\":\"Advisor watcher/SQLite and compiled activation manifests are projections over root sources.\",\"iteration\":1}\n+  ],\n+  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n+    {\"direction\":\"Treat spec-folder metadata generators as skill-root producers\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1}\n+  ],\n@@\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 0,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 0,\n-    \"openQuestions\": 5,\n-    \"resolvedQuestions\": 0,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 1,\n+    \"keyFindings\": 6,\n+    \"openQuestions\": 4,\n+    \"resolvedQuestions\": 1,\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-state.jsonl\n@@\n {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Dimension 1: full inventory and current state of skill/advisor JSON, authored versus generated status, H/S presence, and automation coverage\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":1,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All 6 findings newly establish the bounded type inventory, live 11-root presence/freshness state, and producer-consumer automation map for this lineage.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Treat generate-description.js and backfill-graph-met