{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785306691109,"sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1fh25Vs0fJuKGpDYr26sVD0c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\n - [ ] Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\n@@\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n - [x] What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them? (iteration 1)\n+- [x] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage? (iteration 2)\n@@\n - Consumer and generator tracing separated root identity from advisor projections. (iteration 1)\n+- Field-level consumer tracing distinguished avoidable duplication from load-bearing projections. (iteration 2)\n+- Compiler comments exposed an already-drifted tie-break representation. (iteration 2)\n@@\n - Broad filename discovery mixed unrelated spec-folder continuity JSON with skill-root identity JSON. (iteration 1)\n+- Broad shared-field searches mixed skill metadata with unrelated memory/spec schemas. (iteration 2)\n@@\n - Treat `ci-leaf-manifest-freshness.cjs` as complete fleet-adoption coverage; it discovers committed outputs rather than all `SKILL.md` roots. (iteration 1)\n+- Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data; they preserve serving authority and policy generation. (iteration 2)\n+- Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a generated projection; both serve distinct consumers. (iteration 2)\n+- Remove `grandfatheredFolderMismatch`; it is a validated policy assertion, not dead repetition. (iteration 2)\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Dimension 2, optimization: identify redundant or unused fields, duplicate representations, drift-prone data, consolidation candidates, and fields with no verified consumer across root metadata, advisor projections, and compiled routes.\n+Dimension 3, automation gaps: identify hand-authored or manually synchronized JSON that scaffolding, generators, freshness gates, or reconciliation could own, including coverage gaps in `init_skill.py` and conflicting derived-v2 producers.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n@@\n   \"openQuestions\": [\n-    \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n     \"Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\",\n@@\n     {\n       \"question\": \"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\",\n       \"iteration\": 1,\n       \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-001.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"question\": \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n+      \"iteration\": 2,\n+      \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-002.md\"\n     }\n@@\n-    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f6\",\"summary\":\"Advisor watcher/SQLite and compiled activation manifests are projections over root sources.\",\"iteration\":1}\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-001-f6\",\"summary\":\"Advisor watcher/SQLite and compiled activation manifests are projections over root sources.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f1\",\"summary\":\"TypeScript sync and Python compiler define incompatible derived-v2 shapes consumed differently by the scorer.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f2\",\"summary\":\"sk-doc routerPolicy.tieBreak is an already-drifted duplicate ignored in favor of routerSignals key order.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f3\",\"summary\":\"advisorRouting.packetSkillName duplicates consumed top-level packetSkillName without a verified production reader.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f4\",\"summary\":\"Registry aliases and router vocabulary overlap but retain distinct consumers and need explicit ownership.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f5\",\"summary\":\"Standalone aliases are generated identity copies while hub relocation aliases remain load-bearing.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-002-f6\",\"summary\":\"Five hub description fields lack verified local consumers beyond the enforced four-field identity.\",\"iteration\":2}\n@@\n-    {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1}\n+    {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a projection\",\"iteration\":2},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Remove grandfatheredFolderMismatch as dead repetition\",\"iteration\":2}\n@@\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 1,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 6,\n-    \"openQuestions\": 4,\n-    \"resolvedQuestions\": 1,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n+    \"keyFindings\": 12,\n+    \"openQuestions\": 3,\n+    \"resolvedQuestions\": 2,\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n@@\n-- Progress: 1/5 iterations\n+- Progress: 2/5 iterations\n@@\n | 1 | Inventory and current state | 1.00 | 6 | complete |\n+| 2 | Optimization and consolidation | 0.92 | 6 | complete |\n@@\n-- Answered: 1/5\n-- Remaining: optimization; automation; effectiveness; testing and integration\n+- Answered: 2/5\n+- Remaining: automation; effectiveness; testing and integration\n@@\n-- Ratios: 1.00\n+- Ratios: 1.00 -> 0.92\n@@\n - Output-first leaf freshness is not complete adoption discovery.\n+- Compiled activation manifests are load-bearing generated state, not removable duplication.\n+- Command metadata and mode registries cannot collapse without a projection.\n@@\n-Dimension 2: redundant, unused, duplicated, and drift-prone metadata.\n+Dimension 3: generation, scaffolding, freshness, and reconciliation gaps.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/orchestration-status.log\n@@\n {\"event\":\"progress\",\"label\":\"sol-high\",\"at\":\"2026-07-29T06:16:20Z\",\"duration_ms\":323831,\"loop_type\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-sol-high-1785305275596-oro54j\",\"generation\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"gauges\":{\"iterations\":1,\"elapsed_ms\":323831,\"score\":1.0}}\n+{\"event\":\"progress\",\"label\":\"sol-high\",\"at\":\"2026-07-29T06:22:00Z\",\"duration_ms\":663831,\"loop_type\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-sol-high-1785305275596-oro54j\",\"generation\":1,\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"gauges\":{\"iterations\":2,\"elapsed_ms\":663831,\"score\":0.92}}\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\nM .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/orchestration-status.log","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -7,9 +7,8 @@\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\n - [ ] Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\n - [ ] Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short?\n - [ ] Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n@@ -33,8 +32,9 @@\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n - [x] What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them? (iteration 1)\n+- [x] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage? (iteration 2)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -43,15 +43,18 @@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n - Contract-driven inventory bounded the JSON universe before counting files. (iteration 1)\n - Direct root-gate and freshness-gate execution established current fleet state. (iteration 1)\n - Consumer and generator tracing separated root identity from advisor projections. (iteration 1)\n+- Field-level consumer tracing distinguished avoidable duplication from load-bearing projections. (iteration 2)\n+- Compiler comments exposed an already-drifted tie-break representation. (iteration 2)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n - Broad filename discovery mixed unrelated spec-folder continuity JSON with skill-root identity JSON. (iteration 1)\n+- Broad shared-field searches mixed skill metadata with unrelated memory/spec schemas. (iteration 2)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -65,8 +68,11 @@\n <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n - Treat spec-folder `generate-description.js` and `backfill-graph-metadata.js` as skill-root producers; they own a separate schema. (iteration 1)\n - Treat `ci-leaf-manifest-freshness.cjs` as complete fleet-adoption coverage; it discovers committed outputs rather than all `SKILL.md` roots. (iteration 1)\n+- Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data; they preserve serving authority and policy generation. (iteration 2)\n+- Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a generated projection; both serve distinct consumers. (iteration 2)\n+- Remove `grandfatheredFolderMismatch`; it is a validated policy assertion, not dead repetition. (iteration 2)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -90,9 +96,9 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Dimension 2, optimization: identify redundant or unused fields, duplicate representations, drift-prone data, consolidation candidates, and fields with no verified consumer across root metadata, advisor projections, and compiled routes.\n+Dimension 3, automation gaps: identify hand-authored or manually synchronized JSON that scaffolding, generators, freshness gates, or reconciliation could own, including coverage gaps in `init_skill.py` and conflicting derived-v2 producers.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n \n ---\n \n\nIndex: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n@@ -4,9 +4,8 @@\n \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n \"generation\": 1,\n \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n \"openQuestions\": [\n-  \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n   \"Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\",\n   \"Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short?\",\n   \"Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\"\n ],\n@@ -14,27 +13,41 @@\n   {\n     \"question\": \"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\",\n     \"iteration\": 1,\n     \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-001.md\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"question\": \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n+    \"iteration\": 2,\n+    \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-002.md\"\n   }\n ],\n \"keyFindings\": [\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f1\",\"summary\":\"Eight governed root JSON filenames split across H and S with class-specific authored/generated status.\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f2\",\"summary\":\"The current fleet has seven H and four S roots; all 11 pass root-contract and generated-freshness gates.\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f3\",\"summary\":\"graph-metadata.json is authored identity with a separately generated advisor-maintained derived block.\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f4\",\"summary\":\"Scaffolds emit authored declarations while the root gate owns derivable manifest and S-alias generation.\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f5\",\"summary\":\"The root gate has complete adoption discovery while the older freshness scanner sees committed manifests only.\",\"iteration\":1},\n-  {\"id\":\"iter-001-f6\",\"summary\":\"Advisor watcher/SQLite and compiled activation manifests are projections over root sources.\",\"iteration\":1}\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-001-f6\",\"summary\":\"Advisor watcher/SQLite and compiled activation manifests are projections over root sources.\",\"iteration\":1},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f1\",\"summary\":\"TypeScript sync and Python compiler define incompatible derived-v2 shapes consumed differently by the scorer.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f2\",\"summary\":\"sk-doc routerPolicy.tieBreak is an already-drifted duplicate ignored in favor of routerSignals key order.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f3\",\"summary\":\"advisorRouting.packetSkillName duplicates consumed top-level packetSkillName without a verified production reader.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f4\",\"summary\":\"Registry aliases and router vocabulary overlap but retain distinct consumers and need explicit ownership.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f5\",\"summary\":\"Standalone aliases are generated identity copies while hub relocation aliases remain load-bearing.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f6\",\"summary\":\"Five hub description fields lack verified local consumers beyond the enforced four-field identity.\",\"iteration\":2}\n ],\n \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n   {\"direction\":\"Treat spec-folder metadata generators as skill-root producers\",\"iteration\":1},\n-  {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1}\n+  {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1},\n+  {\"direction\":\"Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"direction\":\"Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a projection\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"direction\":\"Remove grandfatheredFolderMismatch as dead repetition\",\"iteration\":2}\n ],\n \"metrics\": {\n-  \"iterationsCompleted\": 1,\n-  \"keyFindings\": 6,\n-  \"openQuestions\": 4,\n-  \"resolvedQuestions\": 1,\n+  \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n+  \"keyFindings\": 12,\n+  \"openQuestions\": 3,\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": 2,\n   \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n   \"coverageBySources\": {}\n },\n \"rejectedPatterns\": [],\n\nIndex: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n@@ -3,29 +3,32 @@\n ## Lifecycle\n - Session: `fanout-sol-high-1785305275596-oro54j`\n - Status: iterating\n - Stop policy: max-iterations\n-- Progress: 1/5 iterations\n+- Progress: 2/5 iterations\n \