facts; those matches were discarded and later searches were scoped. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -71,8 +73,10 @@\n - Treat `ci-leaf-manifest-freshness.cjs` as complete fleet-adoption coverage; it discovers committed outputs rather than all `SKILL.md` roots. (iteration 1)\n - Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data; they preserve serving authority and policy generation. (iteration 2)\n - Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a generated projection; both serve distinct consumers. (iteration 2)\n - Remove `grandfatheredFolderMismatch`; it is a validated policy assertion, not dead repetition. (iteration 2)\n+- Generate authored H routing semantics from folder structure; vocabulary, edges, aliases, choreography, and activation remain human policy. (iteration 3)\n+- Use same-named spec-folder generators for skill-root identity; their schema and lifecycle are separate. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -96,9 +100,9 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Dimension 3, automation gaps: identify hand-authored or manually synchronized JSON that scaffolding, generators, freshness gates, or reconciliation could own, including coverage gaps in `init_skill.py` and conflicting derived-v2 producers.\n+Dimension 4, effectiveness: trace which authored and generated metadata contributes to advisor candidate selection, lane attribution, hub-mode routing, and fallback behavior; identify high-value intent-signal and integration gaps without redesigning scoring.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n \n ---\n \n","additions":6,"deletions":2},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n@@ -4,9 +4,8 @@\n \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n \"generation\": 1,\n \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n \"openQuestions\": [\n-  \"Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\",\n   \"Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short?\",\n   \"Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\"\n ],\n \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n@@ -18,8 +17,13 @@\n   {\n     \"question\": \"Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage?\",\n     \"iteration\": 2,\n     \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-002.md\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"question\": \"Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked?\",\n+    \"iteration\": 3,\n+    \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-003.md\"\n   }\n ],\n \"keyFindings\": [\n   {\"id\":\"iter-001-f1\",\"summary\":\"Eight governed root JSON filenames split across H and S with class-specific authored/generated status.\",\"iteration\":1},\n@@ -32,22 +36,30 @@\n   {\"id\":\"iter-002-f2\",\"summary\":\"sk-doc routerPolicy.tieBreak is an already-drifted duplicate ignored in favor of routerSignals key order.\",\"iteration\":2},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-002-f3\",\"summary\":\"advisorRouting.packetSkillName duplicates consumed top-level packetSkillName without a verified production reader.\",\"iteration\":2},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-002-f4\",\"summary\":\"Registry aliases and router vocabulary overlap but retain distinct consumers and need explicit ownership.\",\"iteration\":2},\n   {\"id\":\"iter-002-f5\",\"summary\":\"Standalone aliases are generated identity copies while hub relocation aliases remain load-bearing.\",\"iteration\":2},\n-  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f6\",\"summary\":\"Five hub description fields lack verified local consumers beyond the enforced four-field identity.\",\"iteration\":2}\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-002-f6\",\"summary\":\"Five hub description fields lack verified local consumers beyond the enforced four-field identity.\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f1\",\"summary\":\"Scaffolds stop before producing class-required generated manifests and standalone aliases.\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f2\",\"summary\":\"Derived graph metadata has conflicting schemas and the sync writer has no production lifecycle trigger.\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f3\",\"summary\":\"Fleet CI does not validate downstream graph ingestibility, edge/path integrity, or derived freshness.\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f4\",\"summary\":\"Standalone manifest config is mostly conventional boilerplate suitable for defaults plus overrides.\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f5\",\"summary\":\"Hub scaffolding repeats derivable identities across five authored JSON surfaces without reconciliation.\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"id\":\"iter-003-f6\",\"summary\":\"Compiled-route mint/refresh lacks a fleet source-change-to-refresh owner.\",\"iteration\":3}\n ],\n \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n   {\"direction\":\"Treat spec-folder metadata generators as skill-root producers\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1},\n   {\"direction\":\"Delete compiled activation manifests as duplicate route data\",\"iteration\":2},\n   {\"direction\":\"Collapse command metadata into mode registries without a projection\",\"iteration\":2},\n-  {\"direction\":\"Remove grandfatheredFolderMismatch as dead repetition\",\"iteration\":2}\n+  {\"direction\":\"Remove grandfatheredFolderMismatch as dead repetition\",\"iteration\":2},\n+  {\"direction\":\"Generate authored H routing semantics from folder structure\",\"iteration\":3},\n+  {\"direction\":\"Use spec-folder generators for skill-root identity\",\"iteration\":3}\n ],\n \"metrics\": {\n-  \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n-  \"keyFindings\": 12,\n-  \"openQuestions\": 3,\n-  \"resolvedQuestions\": 2,\n+  \"iterationsCompleted\": 3,\n+  \"keyFindings\": 18,\n+  \"openQuestions\": 2,\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": 3,\n   \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n   \"coverageBySources\": {}\n },\n \"rejectedPatterns\": [],\n","additions":19,"deletions":7},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n+++ /Us