\":[\".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/projection-fallback-049-005.vitest.ts:45-106\",\".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/executor-delegation.vitest.ts:177-228\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"iter-005-f5\",\"summary\":\"Compiled source invalidation is behaviorally guarded; watched key-file and delegation alias-cache invalidation are not.\",\"sources\":[\".opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:323-364\",\".opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:1118-1162\",\".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/daemon-watcher-resource-leaks-049-005.vitest.ts:283-312\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"iter-005-f6\",\"summary\":\"sk-doc canaries behaviorally assert all command routes but only two positive natural-language routes and no joined per-mode parent-selection cases.\",\"sources\":[\".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json:5-23\",\".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl:30\"]}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":7,"totalLines":7,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deltas/iter-005.jsonl","time":{"start":1785308272246,"end":1785308272266}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0cc7c8f1a0f71756016a69a4701bd88191847617a7e947e5be"}},"id":"prt_facaa5672001KWDFLX3N5OG01K","sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","messageID":"msg_facaa1fc7001NLrNdsshJODGCw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785308272287,"sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_mnYrIOx4LkNbxjPma4ZreWS5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Progressive Research Notes — sol-high\n2: \n3: ## Iteration 1: Inventory and current state\n4: \n5: - The production skill-root contract governs eight JSON filenames across seven H roots and four S roots; all 11 current roots pass presence/forbidden-file checks and generated artifacts are byte-fresh. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:47-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:372-412]\n6: - Authored files carry identity/policy; `leaf-manifest.json` is generated for both classes and `leaf-aliases.json` is generated only for S. `graph-metadata.json` is authored overall but its `derived` block has dedicated deterministic sync automation. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/lib/skill-root-metadata-contract.cjs:125-152] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/derived/sync.ts:92-138]\n7: - Advisor SQLite/watch state and compiled per-hub activation `manifest.json` are generated projections over root source files, not extra H/S root-contract files. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:228-252] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:391-424]\n8: \n9: The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n10: \n11: ## Iteration 5: Testing and integration\n12: \n13: - Generated manifests/aliases, command metadata, and compiled activation mechanics have behavior-rich tests, while authored identity semantics—especially full graph schema validity—lack one canonical cross-consumer gate. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:296-359] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:406-479]\n14: - No test joins scaffold → generated root gate → advisor ingest/root selection → compiled mode route; existing suites assert genuine behavior but use independent synthetic artifacts at each stage. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/discovery-pipeline-parity.vitest.ts:47-85] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:276-364]\n15: - Highest-priority missing scenarios are natural-language root-to-mode cases for every mode, scaffold-to-ingest happy/failure journeys, watched-key-file and delegation-cache invalidation, and explicit SQLite/filesystem degradation parity. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json:5-23] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/projection-fallback-049-005.vitest.ts:45-106]\n16: \n17: The evidence iterations are complete; workflow-owned final synthesis remains next.\n18: \n19: ## Iteration 4: Effectiveness\n20: \n21: - Root candidate selection consumes SKILL identity/description/keywords plus graph domains, authored intent signals, derived terms, and edges; hub registry/router vocabulary becomes effective only after the parent hub wins. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:173-247] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:173-185]\n22: - The highest-leverage activation gap is that watched derived key files only trigger `indexSkillMetadata()`, whose graph-metadata hash skip prevents those file contents from changing the candidate projection unless another producer refreshes `graph-metadata.json`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:228-252] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:1071-1085]\n23: - Distinctive hub-mode phrases can therefore fail before the active compiled router runs; filesystem fallback additionally drops graph edges and doc triggers, while executor delegation bypasses normal root selection but caches registry/model/archive aliases by workspace without source invalidation. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json:36-49] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:563-720] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts:205-208]\n24: \n25: The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n26: \n27: ## Iteration 3: Automation gaps\n28: \n29: - The create journey stops before class-required generated artifacts exist: standalone scaffolds omit `leaf-manifest.json` and generated aliases, and hub scaffolds omit the manifest; the canonical fleet `--fix` producer is not invoked. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:321-340] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:583-665] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:323-357]\n30: - The highest-risk lifecycle gap is `graph-metadata.json.derived`: scaffolds emit a legacy shape, TypeScript sync and Python compile enforce incompatible v2 shapes, and the sync writer is not connected to the watcher/rebuild production path. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:270-294] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:306-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:425-426]\n31: - Automation should target boilerplate/projections—standalone config defaults, repeated hub identities, generated manifests/aliases, derived labels, and compiled freshness—while retaining authored routing vocabulary, graph relationships, relocation aliases, command choreography, and activation authority. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:95-127] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/lib/skill-root-metadata-contract.cjs:125-152] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:650-753]\n32: \n33: The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n34: \n35: ## Iteration 2: Optimization\n36: \n37: - The highest-leverage consolidation is the conflicting derived-v2 contract: TypeScript sync emits `keywords` plus provenance/lifecycle fields, while the Python compiler requires `key_topics`, `entities`, `causal_summary`, and legacy timestamps; the scorer consumes `key_topics` rather than sync's `keywords`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:300-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:658-685]\n38: - Confirmed avoidable drift surfaces are sk-doc's ignored `routerPolicy.tieBreak` copy and nested `advisorRouting.packetSkillName`; top-level packet identity remains consumed. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:188-195] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts:160-174]\n39: - Standalone aliases are generated identity copies that could be derived