 standalone scaffolds omit `leaf-manifest.json` and generated aliases, and hub scaffolds omit the manifest; the canonical fleet `--fix` producer is not invoked. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:321-340] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:583-665] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:323-357]\n- The highest-risk lifecycle gap is `graph-metadata.json.derived`: scaffolds emit a legacy shape, TypeScript sync and Python compile enforce incompatible v2 shapes, and the sync writer is not connected to the watcher/rebuild production path. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:270-294] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:306-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:425-426]\n- Automation should target boilerplate/projections—standalone config defaults, repeated hub identities, generated manifests/aliases, derived labels, and compiled freshness—while retaining authored routing vocabulary, graph relationships, relocation aliases, command choreography, and activation authority. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:95-127] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/lib/skill-root-metadata-contract.cjs:125-152] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:650-753]\n\nThe full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n\n## Iteration 2: Optimization\n\n- The highest-leverage consolidation is the conflicting derived-v2 contract: TypeScript sync emits `keywords` plus provenance/lifecycle fields, while the Python compiler requires `key_topics`, `entities`, `causal_summary`, and legacy timestamps; the scorer consumes `key_topics` rather than sync's `keywords`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:300-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:658-685]\n- Confirmed avoidable drift surfaces are sk-doc's ignored `routerPolicy.tieBreak` copy and nested `advisorRouting.packetSkillName`; top-level packet identity remains consumed. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:188-195] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts:160-174]\n- Standalone aliases are generated identity copies that could be derived in memory after consumer migration; hub aliases, compiled activation manifests, command metadata, and explicit mismatch assertions remain load-bearing in their current contracts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:205-249] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:650-735]\n\nThe full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":41,"totalLines":41,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md","time":{"start":1785308272274,"end":1785308272285}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0cc7c8f1a0f71756016a69a4701be48191ab8d6fa41c0de8b3"}},"id":"prt_facaa56790013d6FedU6DmRTJo","sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","messageID":"msg_facaa1fc7001NLrNdsshJODGCw"}}
