te-manifest.cjs`\n+- `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs`\n+- `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs`\n+- `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation/sk-doc/manifest.json`\n+\n+## Tests And CI\n+- `.opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs`\n+- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/discovery-pipeline-parity.vitest.ts`\n+- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/projection-fallback-049-005.vitest.ts`\n+- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/projection-freshness.vitest.ts`\n+- `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/executor-delegation.vitest.ts`\n+- `.opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs`\n+- `.opencode/bin/compiled-routing-foundation.vitest.ts`\n+- `.github/workflows/routing-registry-drift.yml`\n+\n+## Evidence Artifacts\n+- `iterations/iteration-001.md` through `iterations/iteration-005.md`\n+- `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` through `deltas/iter-005.jsonl`\n+- `deep-research-state.jsonl`\n+- `findings-registry.json`\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -6,10 +6,9 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n-\n-- [ ] Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\n+[All five key questions answered]\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -33,8 +32,9 @@\n - [x] What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them? (iteration 1)\n - [x] Which fields or files are redundant, unused, duplicated, or drift-prone, and what consolidation has the highest leverage? (iteration 2)\n - [x] Which hand-authored JSON and validation steps could be generated, scaffolded, or automatically checked? (iteration 3)\n - [x] Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short? (iteration 4)\n+- [x] Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage? (iteration 5)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -48,8 +48,9 @@\n - Compiler comments exposed an already-drifted tie-break representation. (iteration 2)\n - Lifecycle tracing from scaffold through ingest exposed ownership handoffs and missing end-to-end automation. (iteration 3)\n - Phrase-level tracing from watch through projection and compiled routing exposed activation gaps. (iteration 4)\n - Targeted live advisor probes confirmed both working and missed metadata boundaries. (iteration 4)\n+- Reading assertions rather than test names separated strong stage-local tests from missing lifecycle seams. (iteration 5)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -58,8 +59,9 @@\n - Broad filename discovery mixed unrelated spec-folder continuity JSON with skill-root identity JSON. (iteration 1)\n - Broad shared-field searches mixed skill metadata with unrelated memory/spec schemas. (iteration 2)\n - One broad production search crossed into sibling artifacts; those matches were discarded and later searches were scoped. (iteration 3)\n - Committed executable and narrative evaluation baselines report different versioned totals and cannot be merged. (iteration 4)\n+- Broad test-name discovery produced unrelated phase fixtures and required narrowing to stage entrypoints. (iteration 5)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -81,8 +83,10 @@\n - Use same-named spec-folder generators for skill-root identity; their schema and lifecycle are separate. (iteration 3)\n - Treat hub registry/router vocabulary as normal root-selection input; it becomes visible only after parent selection. (iteration 4)\n - Treat key-file watch activation as content regeneration; unchanged graph metadata is reindexed as unchanged. (iteration 4)\n - Redesign lane weights for metadata activation misses; the missing projection is upstream of fusion. (iteration 4)\n+- Treat fixture presence as behavioral coverage; several suites assert real behavior, but cross-stage scenarios remain absent. (iteration 5)\n+- Treat isolated discovery parity as complete ingest parity; it preserves a deliberate depth divergence and does not prove recommendation equivalence. (iteration 5)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n ---\n \n@@ -106,9 +110,9 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Dimension 5, testing and integration: map per-JSON unit and CI coverage plus end-to-end scaffold-to-gate-to-ingest-to-root-selection-to-compiled-route behavior, including fallback parity, cache invalidation, freshness, and natural-language per-mode scenarios.\n+Synthesis complete. Use the ranked opportunity map in `research.md`; no implementation is authorized by this lineage.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n \n ---\n \n","additions":7,"deletions":3},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/findings-registry.json\n@@ -3,11 +3,9 @@\n   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n   \"generation\": 1,\n   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n-  \"openQuestions\": [\n-    \"Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\"\n-  ],\n+  \"openQuestions\": [],\n   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n     {\n       \"question\": \"What JSON types exist, which are authored versus generated, where are they present for H and S roots, and what automation covers them?\",\n       \"iteration\": 1,\n@@ -26,8 +24,13 @@\n     {\n       \"question\": \"Which metadata and intent signals actually drive advisor routing, and where does routing effectiveness fall short?\",\n       \"iteration\": 4,\n       \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-004.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"question\": \"Which JSON surfaces lack unit, CI, freshness, scaffold-to-ingest, and end-to-end routing coverage?\",\n+      \"iteration\": 5,\n+      \"evidence\": \"iterations/iteration-005.md\"\n     }\n   ],\n   \"keyFindings\": [\n     {\"id\":\"iter-001-f1\",\"summary\":\"Eight governed root JSON filenames split across H and S with class-specific authored/generated status.\",\"iteration\":1},\n@@ -52,9 +55,15 @@\n     {\"id\":\"iter-004-f2\",\"summary\":\"Normal root selection consumes SKILL and graph projection fields, not hub registry/router or leaf JSON.\",\"iteration\":4},\n     {\"id\":\"iter-004-f3\",\"summary\":\"High-specificity hub vocabulary is invisible until parent selection, producing confirmed natural-language misses.\",\"iteration\":4},\n     {\"id\":\"iter-004-f4\",\"summary\":\"Filesystem fallback retains direct root fields but drops graph edges and doc-trigger projections.\",\"iteration\":4},\n     {\"id\":\"iter-004-f5\",\"summary\":\"Executor delegation consumes hub aliases but memoizes them without source-change invalidation.\",\"iteration\":4},\n-    {\"id\":\"iter-004-f6\",\"summary\":\"Compiled sk-doc routing is active while committed evaluation supports moderate version-sensitive root accuracy.\",\"iteration\":4}\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-004-f6\",\"summary\":\"Compiled sk-doc routing is active while committed evaluation supports moderate version-sensitive root accuracy.\",\"iteration\":4},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f1\",\"summary\":\"Generated artifacts and command metadata have behavior-rich coverage; authored identity lacks one canonical full-schema gate.\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f2\",\"summary\":\"No test joins scaffold, generated gate, advisor ingest, root selection, and compiled mode selection.\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f3\",\"summary\":\"Failure handling is deep inside stages but does not propagate failures across lifecycle seams.\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f4\",\"summary\":\"Filesystem fallback tests prove availability and warnings, not lane or recommendation parity.\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f5\",\"summary\":\"Compiled invalidation is guarded; watched-key and delegation-cache invalidation are not.\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"id\":\"iter-005-f6\",\"summary\":\"Canaries cover all command routes but only two positive natural-language routes and no joined per-mode parent cases.\",\"iteration\":5}\n   ],\n   \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n     {\"direction\":\"Treat spec-folder metadata generators as skill-root producers\",\"iteration\":1},\n     {\"direction\":\"Treat output-first leaf-manifest freshness as complete adoption coverage\",\"iteration\":1},\n@@ -64,19 +73,23 @@\n     {\"direction\":\"Generate authored H routing semantics from folder structure\",\"iteration\":3},\n     {\"direction\":\"Use spec-folder generators for skill-root identity\",\"iteration\":3},\n     {\"direction\":\"Treat hub router vocabulary as normal advisor root-selection input\",\"iteration\":4},\n     {\"direction\":\"Treat key-file watch activation as derived-content refresh\",\"iteration\":4},\n-    {\"direction\":\"Redesign scorer weights for upstream metadata activation gaps\",\"iteration\":4}\n+    {\"direction\":\"Redesign scorer weights for upstream metadata activation gaps\",\"iteration\":4},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Treat fixture presence as behavioral coverage\",\"iteration\":5},\n+    {\"direction\":\"Treat isolated discovery parity as complete ingest parity\",\"iteration\":5}\n   ],\n   \"metrics\": {\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 4,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 24,\n-    \"openQuestions\": 1,\n-    \"resolvedQuestions\": 4,\n-    \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 5,\n+    \"keyFindings\": 30,\n+    \"openQuestions\": 0,\n+    \"resolvedQuestions\": 5,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0.082,\n     \"coverageBySources\": {}\n   },\n   \"rejectedPatterns\": [],\n   \"promotedIdeas\": [],\n   \"saturatedDirections\": [],\n-  \"pivotLineage\": []\n+  \"pivotLineage\": [],\n+  \"stopReason\": \"maxIterationsReached\",\n+  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-07-29T06:40:00Z\"\n }\n","additions":24,"deletions":11},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-dashboard.md\n@@ -1,26 +1,27 @@\n # Deep Research Dashboard - sol-high\n \n ## Lifecycle\n - Session: `fanout-sol-high-1785305275596-oro54j`\n-- Status: iterating\n+- Status: complete\n - Stop policy: max-iterations\n-- Progress: 4/5 iterations\n+- Progress: 5/5 iterations\n \n ## Iteration Table\n | Run | Focus | newInfoRatio | Findings | Status |\n |---|---|---:|---:|---|\n | 1 | Inventory and current state | 1.00 | 6 | complete |\n | 2 | Optimization and consolidation | 0.92 | 6 | complete |\n | 3 | Automation and lifecycle ownership | 0.83 | 6 | complete |\n | 4 | Metadata-to-route effectiveness | 0.92 | 6 | complete |\n+| 5 | Testing and integration | 0.92 | 6 | complete |\n \n ## Question Status\n-- Answered: 4/5\n-- Remaining: testing and integration\n+- Answered: 5/5\n+- Remaining: none\n \n ## Convergence Trend\n-- Ratios: 1.00 -> 0.92 -> 0.83 -> 0.92\n+- Ratios: 1.00 -> 0.92 -> 0.83 -> 0.92 -> 0.92\n - Convergence is telemetry only before iteration 5.\n \n ## Dead Ends\n - Spec-folder metadata generators are not skill-root producers.\n@@ -29,11 +30,18 @@\n - Command metadata and mode registries cannot collapse without a projection.\n - Authored H routing policy cannot be generated safely from folder shape.\n - Rich hub vocabulary cannot recover root-selection misses after the wrong parent wins.\n - Key-file watch events do not regenerate unchanged graph metadata.\n+- Fixture presence is not equivalent to cross-stage behavioral coverage.\n \n ## Next Focus\n-Dimension 5: per-JSON testing and full lifecycle integration coverage.\n+Final synthesis and ranked opportunity map in `research.md`.\n \n ## Active Risks\n - Code graph unavailable; source tracing is direct.\n - No packet resource map; coverage must be established from the contract and source inventory.\n+\n+## Completion\n+- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`\n+- Questions answered: 5/5\n+- Findings: 30\n+- All five mechanical iteration gates passed.\n","additions":14,"deletions":6},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-config.json","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-config.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/deep-research-config.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk