{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785308402044,"sessionID":"ses_053835f44ffewNv42EZbxtppsV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_LiTinXQr9NYcHhiFdhI1sKoQ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Delete File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n@@ -1,41 +0,0 @@\n-# Progressive Research Notes — sol-high\n-\n-## Iteration 1: Inventory and current state\n-\n-- The production skill-root contract governs eight JSON filenames across seven H roots and four S roots; all 11 current roots pass presence/forbidden-file checks and generated artifacts are byte-fresh. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md:47-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:372-412]\n-- Authored files carry identity/policy; `leaf-manifest.json` is generated for both classes and `leaf-aliases.json` is generated only for S. `graph-metadata.json` is authored overall but its `derived` block has dedicated deterministic sync automation. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/lib/skill-root-metadata-contract.cjs:125-152] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/derived/sync.ts:92-138]\n-- Advisor SQLite/watch state and compiled per-hub activation `manifest.json` are generated projections over root source files, not extra H/S root-contract files. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:228-252] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:391-424]\n-\n-The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n-\n-## Iteration 5: Testing and integration\n-\n-- Generated manifests/aliases, command metadata, and compiled activation mechanics have behavior-rich tests, while authored identity semantics—especially full graph schema validity—lack one canonical cross-consumer gate. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:296-359] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/tests/skill-root-metadata-contract.test.cjs:406-479]\n-- No test joins scaffold → generated root gate → advisor ingest/root selection → compiled mode route; existing suites assert genuine behavior but use independent synthetic artifacts at each stage. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/discovery-pipeline-parity.vitest.ts:47-85] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs:276-364]\n-- Highest-priority missing scenarios are natural-language root-to-mode cases for every mode, scaffold-to-ingest happy/failure journeys, watched-key-file and delegation-cache invalidation, and explicit SQLite/filesystem degradation parity. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json:5-23] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/projection-fallback-049-005.vitest.ts:45-106]\n-\n-The evidence iterations are complete; workflow-owned final synthesis remains next.\n-\n-## Iteration 4: Effectiveness\n-\n-- Root candidate selection consumes SKILL identity/description/keywords plus graph domains, authored intent signals, derived terms, and edges; hub registry/router vocabulary becomes effective only after the parent hub wins. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:173-247] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:173-185]\n-- The highest-leverage activation gap is that watched derived key files only trigger `indexSkillMetadata()`, whose graph-metadata hash skip prevents those file contents from changing the candidate projection unless another producer refreshes `graph-metadata.json`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:228-252] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:1071-1085]\n-- Distinctive hub-mode phrases can therefore fail before the active compiled router runs; filesystem fallback additionally drops graph edges and doc triggers, while executor delegation bypasses normal root selection but caches registry/model/archive aliases by workspace without source invalidation. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json:36-49] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:563-720] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts:205-208]\n-\n-The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n-\n-## Iteration 3: Automation gaps\n-\n-- The create journey stops before class-required generated artifacts exist: standalone scaffolds omit `leaf-manifest.json` and generated aliases, and hub scaffolds omit the manifest; the canonical fleet `--fix` producer is not invoked. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:321-340] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:583-665] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:323-357]\n-- The highest-risk lifecycle gap is `graph-metadata.json.derived`: scaffolds emit a legacy shape, TypeScript sync and Python compile enforce incompatible v2 shapes, and the sync writer is not connected to the watcher/rebuild production path. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:270-294] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:306-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/daemon/watcher.ts:425-426]\n-- Automation should target boilerplate/projections—standalone config defaults, repeated hub identities, generated manifests/aliases, derived labels, and compiled freshness—while retaining authored routing vocabulary, graph relationships, relocation aliases, command choreography, and activation authority. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:95-127] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/lib/skill-root-metadata-contract.cjs:125-152] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:650-753]\n-\n-The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n-\n-## Iteration 2: Optimization\n-\n-- The highest-leverage consolidation is the conflicting derived-v2 contract: TypeScript sync emits `keywords` plus provenance/lifecycle fields, while the Python compiler requires `key_topics`, `entities`, `causal_summary`, and legacy timestamps; the scorer consumes `key_topics` rather than sync's `keywords`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/schemas/skill-derived-v2.ts:35-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_graph_compiler.py:300-325] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/projection.ts:658-685]\n-- Confirmed avoidable drift surfaces are sk-doc's ignored `routerPolicy.tieBreak` copy and nested `advisorRouting.packetSkillName`; top-level packet identity remains consumed. [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:188-195] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts:160-174]\n-- Standalone aliases are generated identity copies that could be derived in memory after consumer migration; hub aliases, compiled activation manifests, command metadata, and explicit mismatch assertions remain load-bearing in their current contracts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:205-249] [SOURCE: .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs:650-735]\n-\n-The full five-dimension synthesis and ranked opportunity map remain deferred until iteration 5.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md","type":"delete","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/029-skill-json-optimization-research/research/lineages/sol-high/research.md